This directory is a REDISTRIBUTED third-party model artifact, vendored into the
coremlit repository so that CI and every clone have it without a download step.
It is NOT coremlit code and is NOT covered by coremlit's own MIT OR Apache-2.0
dual license. Its terms are MIT, recorded in full below.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What this artifact is

  Artifact   silero-vad-unified-256ms-v6.2.1.mlmodelc  (compiled CoreML model)
  Source     https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/silero-vad-coreml
  Revision   b419383c55c110e2c9271fa6ee0ea83d03c70d96
  Upstream   Silero VAD — https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
  Via        onnx-community/silero-vad (the conversion's declared base model)

The bytes here are FluidInference's CoreML conversion of Silero VAD, copied
verbatim from that repository at that revision. Nothing was modified. The
per-file SHA-256 of every file that came from the Hub is pinned in
crates/coremlit/tests/vad/model_io.rs and re-verified by a model-gated test;
this LICENSE file is coremlit's own addition and is not part of the download.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
License provenance — stated precisely, because two of the three links in the
chain assert MIT without shipping a license file

  1. Silero VAD (upstream, snakers4/silero-vad) — MIT, and it SHIPS the MIT
     text with the copyright line `Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team`.
     That is the notice reproduced below.

  2. onnx-community/silero-vad (the conversion's declared base model) — MIT,
     and it ships a LICENSE file whose text and copyright line are byte-
     identical to upstream's. No additional claimant appears.

  3. FluidInference/silero-vad-coreml (the artifact vendored here) — asserts
     MIT in three places at the pinned revision: the model card's
     `license: mit` front matter, the Hugging Face `license:mit` tag, and the
     README's `**License:** MIT` line. It ships NO LICENSE file and states NO
     copyright line, so no copyright is asserted on their behalf here; the only
     attribution the artifact itself carries is its metadata.json
     `author` field, verbatim: `Fluid Infernece + Silero Team` (their spelling).

MIT's obligation is to preserve "the above copyright notice and this permission
notice". The only copyright notice asserted anywhere in this chain is the
Silero Team's, and it is reproduced in full below. The same record, with the
surrounding attribution for every other model coremlit touches, is in the
repository-root NOTICE, sections 1-2.

